<div id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Without this addition, the original diagram represents a region in
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{1,2}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{1,2}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(i,j)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(i,j)=2</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(i,j)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(i,j)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;j</annotation></semantics></math> for all pairs <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}\subset\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}\subset\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We
add <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(i,5)=\beta(5,i)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(i,5)=\beta(5,i)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,4</annotation></semantics></math>, and we add <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(3,5)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(3,5)=1</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem7.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(3,5)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(3,5)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p18.1" class="ltx_p">As in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, for each
<math id="S6.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> we define <math id="S6.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(i)</annotation></semantics></math> as the position of the leftmost
element of the continuous component of <math id="S6.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We call the resulting
<math id="S6.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f(1),f(2),\ldots,f(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f(1),f(2),\ldots,f(n))</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="S6.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-parking function</span> of the
region. For example, in Example <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem7" title="Example 6.7. ‣ 6. Extended Shi arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a> we have <math id="S6.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=2</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S6.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(2)=f(4)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(2)=f(4)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(3)=f(5)=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(3)=f(5)=6</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof of Athanasiadis and Linusson
showing that we may reconstruct the diagram from its <math id="S6.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-parking
function still applies: we insert the components in increasing order of
the position of the left end of their components and we interlace the
rest of the inserted component with the already inserted components in
such a way that no pair of nested arcs is formed. It seems hard to
characterize the resulting <math id="S6.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-functions in general, but they can be
easily visualized, using an idea implicit in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Ch1. Exercise
(32)(c)]</cite>.</p>
</div>
