<div id="S7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We identify the <math id="S7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th up step from the right with the variable
<math id="S7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\pi(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\pi(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the level of the lower end of the up step with
<math id="S7.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\pi(i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\pi(i))</annotation></semantics></math>. We use this <span id="S7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">level function</span> <math id="S7.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:\{1,2,\ldots,n\}\rightarrow\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:\{1,2,\ldots,n\}\rightarrow\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> to define the weight function,
as follows.</p>
<table id="S7.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\pi(i),\pi(j))=\begin{cases}\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))\in[1-a,a-1]$}\\
-\infty&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&lt;1-a$}\\
a-1&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&gt;a-1$}\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i),\pi(j))=\begin{cases}\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))\in[1-a,a-1]$}\\
-\infty&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&lt;1-a$}\\
a-1&amp;\mbox{if $\ell(\pi(j))-\ell(\pi(i))&gt;a-1$}\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that the notation <math id="S7.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\pi(i),\pi(j))=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i),\pi(j))=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the case
when there is no arrow <math id="S7.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(i)\rightarrow\pi(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(i)\rightarrow\pi(j)</annotation></semantics></math> in the corresponding
weighted digraph, only an arrow <math id="S7.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(i)\leftarrow\pi(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(i)\leftarrow\pi(j)</annotation></semantics></math> of weight
<math id="S7.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Equation (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) defines exactly one of <math id="S7.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S7.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(j,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(j,i)</annotation></semantics></math> for each pair <math id="S7.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may uniquely extend this definition
to all ordered pairs using the rule</p>
<table id="S7.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(i,j)=\begin{cases}-1-w(j,i)&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)\in[1-a,a-2]$}\\
-\infty&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)=a-1$}\\
a-1&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)=-\infty$}\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(i,j)=\begin{cases}-1-w(j,i)&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)\in[1-a,a-2]$}\\
-\infty&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)=a-1$}\\
a-1&amp;\mbox{if $w(j,i)=-\infty$}\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Clearly we obtain the weight function of a valid weighted digraph.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equations (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S7.E3" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>) define an <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-acyclic
weighted digraph.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a directed cycle <math id="S7.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi(i_{1}),\pi(i,2),\ldots,\pi(i_{k})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi(i_{1}),\pi(i,2),\ldots,\pi(i_{k})))</annotation></semantics></math>. In the
proof we add the indices modulo <math id="S7.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, that is we set <math id="S7.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k+1}=i_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k+1}=i_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S7.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{s}&lt;i_{s+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{s}&lt;i_{s+1}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="S7.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})\leq\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))-\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})\leq\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))-\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S7.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{s}&gt;i_{s+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{s}&gt;i_{s+1}</annotation></semantics></math> we must have
<math id="S7.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\pi(i_{s+1}),\pi(i_{s}))&lt;a-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i_{s+1}),\pi(i_{s}))&lt;a-1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise
<math id="S7.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1}))=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1}))=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Hence
we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-1-w(\pi(i_{s+1}),\pi(i_{s}))=-1-(\ell(\pi(i_{s}))-\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-1-w(\pi(i_{s+1}),\pi(i_{s}))=-1-(\ell(\pi(i_{s}))-\ell(\pi(i_{s+1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S7.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\ell(\pi(i_{s+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{s})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\ell(\pi(i_{s+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize <math id="S7.p7.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})\leq\ell(\pi(i_{s+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\pi(i_{s}),\pi(i_{s+1})\leq\ell(\pi(i_{s+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> always holds, hence the total weight
of the cycle is at most <math id="S7.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{k}(\ell(\pi(i_{j+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{j}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{k}(\ell(\pi(i_{j+1})-\ell(\pi(i_{j}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The sum is strictly negative
because there is at least one <math id="S7.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{s}&gt;i_{s+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{s}&gt;i_{s+1}</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.3</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We call the <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-acyclic valid weighted digraph associated to
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> by the Equations (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>)
and (<a href="#S7.E3" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>) the weighted digraph encoded by <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.4</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider weighted digraph encoded by
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. The total order of gains <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\gamma\circ\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\gamma\circ\pi</annotation></semantics></math>
is the order of the labels <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(1),\ldots,\pi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(1),\ldots,\pi(n)</annotation></semantics></math> in increasing order of
their levels, where <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is listed before <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(j)</annotation></semantics></math> if
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\pi(i))=\ell(\pi(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\pi(i))=\ell(\pi(j))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> hold.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For example, for the labeled lattice path shown in
Figure <a href="#S7.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we get <math id="S7.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=142635" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>142635</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=142635</annotation></semantics></math>. It is an immediate
consequence of Equation (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>)
that <math id="S7.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\sigma(i),\sigma(j))\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\sigma(i),\sigma(j))\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="S7.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>, and there is
exactly one permutation with this property.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.5</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the weighted digraph encoded by <math id="S7.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> the gain function is
the level function: we have <math id="S7.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(i))=\ell(\sigma(i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(i))=\ell(\sigma(i))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by induction on <math id="S7.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S7.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> we have
<math id="S7.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(1))=\ell(\sigma(1))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(1))=\ell(\sigma(1))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that
<math id="S7.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(i))=\ell(\sigma(i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(i))=\ell(\sigma(i))</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="S7.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> and let us compute
<math id="S7.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(j))</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 4.10. ‣ 4. Separated deformations and the weak triangle inequality ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a> there is a <math id="S7.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfying <math id="S7.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(j))=g(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+w(\sigma(j^{\prime}),\sigma(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(j))=g(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+w(\sigma(j^{\prime}),\sigma(j))</annotation></semantics></math>. By the
induction hypothesis <math id="S7.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(j^{\prime}))=\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(j^{\prime}))=\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math> holds, hence we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\sigma(j))=\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+w(\sigma(j^{\prime}),\sigma(j))\leq\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+\ell(\sigma(j))-\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))=\ell(\sigma(j))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\sigma(j))=\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+w(\sigma(j^{\prime}),\sigma(j))\leq\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))+\ell(\sigma(j))-\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime}))=\ell(\sigma(j)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, in an <math id="S7.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>-Catalan path, between two consecutive
up steps the level increases by at most <math id="S7.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-1</annotation></semantics></math> (it may also decrease all
the way to zero). If we project all up
steps to the horizontal axis, we obtain a set of intervals whose union
is an interval of integers. Therefore, between any two up steps there is
such a sequence of up steps that the level function can increase by at
most <math id="S7.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-1</annotation></semantics></math> between two subsequent up steps <math id="S7.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,a-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,a-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence there is at
least one up step labeled with <math id="S7.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(j^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(j^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> preceding the up step labeled
with <math id="S7.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(j)</annotation></semantics></math> whose level is in the interval
<math id="S7.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-a+1+\ell(\sigma(j)),\ell(\sigma(j))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-a+1+\ell(\sigma(j)),\ell(\sigma(j))]</annotation></semantics></math>. By
Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 7.4. ‣ 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a> <math id="S7.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime\prime}&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime\prime}&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> holds, hence by Equation (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In 7. The 𝑎-Catalan arrangements ‣ Labeling regions in deformations of graphical arrangements" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) we have
<math id="S7.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\sigma(j^{\prime\prime}),\sigma(j))=\ell(\sigma(j))-\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\sigma(j^{\prime\prime}),\sigma(j))=\ell(\sigma(j))-\ell(\sigma(j^{\prime\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining
this with the induction hypothesis we also obtain</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

